<title>FRANCE: French budget deficit 60 bln Ffr end-Jan - finmin.</title>
<headline>French budget deficit 60 bln Ffr end-Jan - finmin.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French budget deficit at the end of January stood at 60 billion francs, the finance ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>The figure compared to a deficit of 69.6 billion at the end of January 1996, it said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following breakdown of budget receipts: (figures in billions, year on year changes in percent, 1997 year forecast):</p>
<p> REVENUES			end Jan 97  Jan 96  pct	 1997</p>
<p> Net tax receipts		 102.5     99.2   3.3    1,395.3</p>
<p>  of which: -- income tax	17.2     16.9   1.8	291.8</p>
<p>  -- net company tax		0.3	1.3 -76.9	144.8</p>
<p>  -- petrol duties		  8.8	9.2  -4.3	151.9</p>
<p>  -- net Value Added Tax	 65.8     62.2   5.8	635.2</p>
<p>  -- miscellaneous		 10.4	9.6   8.3	171.6</p>
<p> Non-tax receipts		   5.9	6.4  -7.8	155.1</p>
<p> Local authority, EU charges  -29.0    -24.6  17.9     -253.9</p>
<p> General budget receipts	 85.3     87.2  -2.2    1,296.5</p>
<p> SPENDING			end Jan 97  Jan 96  pct</p>
<p> Ordinary civil spending	114.1    115.8  -1.5</p>
<p> of which debt		     11.3     17.3 -34.7</p>
<p> Capital civil spending	   6.2	4.4  40.9</p>
<p> Ordinary military spending    13.3     13.4  -0.7</p>
<p> Capital military spending	7.6     10.3 -26.2</p>
<p> TOTAL BUDGET SPENDING	  141.2    143.9  -1.9</p>
<p>BALANCE</p>
<p> Total net spending	     141.2    143.9  -1.9</p>
<p> Total net receipts		85.3     87.2  -2.2</p>
<p> General budget deficit	 -55.9    -56.7</p>
<p> Special Treasury Accounts     -4.1    -12.9</p>
<p> TOTAL CENTRAL GOVT DEFICIT   -60.0    -69.6</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5542</p>
